[[File:Labyrinth unit loss.png|A table of average unit losses|class=large-image]]

Without factoring in losing or quitting stages, the number of trapped units in a complete run of the Underground Labyrinth can technically be as low as 335 (minimum traps and 99 rescues) or as high as 632 (maximum traps and 0 rescues). Realistically however, the total number of lost units will hover somewhere around 473.6 (average traps, 59.4 rescues) with higher or lower losses than this becoming exponentially less probable to the point of statistical impossibility.

[[File:Labyrinth unit loss plot.png|A plot of expected units lost with respect to levels|class=large-image]]

===List of Stages===
{{:Underground Labyrinth/Stages}}
Due to the difference in possible stages (113) and used stages per event (100), a total of 3 Floor 10 stages, 2 Floor 20/30 stages, 3 Floor 40/50/60 stages, 4 Floor 70/80/90/99 stages, and 1 stage between 61 ~ 98 (excluding multiples of 10) will go unused in each Underground Labyrinth.

==List of Floors==
Each stage has a drop reward as listed in the table below. The rewards drop at a 100% chance on the 99th floor and floors that are multiples of 10, and a 50% chance on all other floors.
{{:Underground Labyrinth/Floors}}

==Ranking Rewards==
Final rank is primarily determined by the number of floors cleared, but in cases where players have the same floors cleared the number of remaining units will be used as a tie breaker. The final rank will determine rewards, similar to how in the [[Ranking Dojo]] higher percentiles reap higher rewards. After the event ends, the highest-tier Underground Labyrinth medal the player qualified for will be added to the upper-left corner of their [[Battle Cats Officers' Club]] card.
